That's the first principle.

00:39:16.280 --> 00:39:21.520
Principle number two leads from this idea
of trading for income.

00:39:21.540 --> 00:39:32.180
Now, we've already seen in previous videos
that all successful professional traders,
in fact, all professional traders, have
basic salaries already.

00:39:32.780 --> 00:39:35.920
No one trades for income, and no one takes
income from their trading account.

00:39:36.300 --> 00:39:39.100
So why do retail traders think they can
trade for income?

00:39:39.600 --> 00:39:42.160
Well, it's because of marketing and
misinformation.

00:39:42.940 --> 00:39:46.100
Everybody likes to tell you what you want
to hear.

00:39:46.320 --> 00:39:55.720
And what you want to hear is that trading
is easy, and you can make money every
month, and you can supplement your income,
or do it full-time, and earn a good income
from it.

00:39:56.380 --> 00:40:02.520
Unfortunately, every professional trader
knows this isn't true, and that's why they
have basic salaries.

00:40:03.960 --> 00:40:09.340
So trading for income doesn't exist in the
professional world, so why should it exist
in the retail trader world?

00:40:10.000 --> 00:40:14.780
This is a very, very important principle
that you need to take on board.

00:40:15.560 --> 00:40:23.640
Because this becomes a situation where
professional traders, because they know
this, they look at the market in a very
different way.

00:40:24.860 --> 00:40:41.100
And this is the way you should be looking
at the market, because the way a
professional trader looks at the market is
that the market dictates the opportunities
that you have as a trader over any given
time horizon.

00:40:41.660 --> 00:40:46.080
Whether it's one day, one week, one month,
a year, it doesn't matter.

00:40:46.640 --> 00:40:49.860
The market tells you what your
opportunities are, not the other way
around.

00:40:50.320 --> 00:40:56.900
You don't tell the market how much money
you can make in a day, week, month, year.

00:40:57.120 --> 00:40:58.400
The market tells you.

00:40:59.100 --> 00:41:10.800
So let's go back to this example of the
EURUSD, where, for example, you're about
to trade this market, but you realise that
the EURUSD hasn't moved at all.

00:41:11.140 --> 00:41:12.800
So it's a theoretical example.

00:41:13.560 --> 00:41:17.480
The EURUSD hasn't moved at all for the
last year.

00:41:19.080 --> 00:41:21.720
So it's been the same price every day for
the last year.

00:41:21.960 --> 00:41:26.660
Well, all that's going to happen is you're
going to buy and sell the EURUSD at the
same price.

00:41:27.460 --> 00:41:30.440
You're never going to make money, and
therefore you can't make an income.

00:41:31.500 --> 00:41:32.520
You can't make a profit.

00:41:32.820 --> 00:41:33.620
You can't make a loss.

00:41:33.880 --> 00:41:34.640
You can't make anything.

00:41:34.860 --> 00:41:35.560
You can't do anything.

00:41:36.580 --> 00:41:41.980
This is what all professional traders
know, and it's basic, but everybody misses
this situation.

00:41:43.260 --> 00:41:56.740
Everybody thinks trading is for income,
when professional traders know, and this
is the important principle, that the
market dictates your opportunities, and
the volatility of that market specifically
dictates those opportunities.

00:41:57.880 --> 00:42:05.040
So essentially, your job as a trader, and
